Must-do (client-architecture.md §11):

- W5: move native/bridge.ts to platform/native/ at bridge version 2 (§5.10), then delete native/
  and its lint exemption in lint/rules.js.
- L4 (daemon): an `input` refusal (`busy`, `inputTooLarge`) names no request, so the client cannot
  report which typed characters were refused. Paste refusals now carry their request id; the
  terminal's short input batch remains necessary until input has its own result contract.
- Phone dock (P3a): landscape and keyboard-up behaviour need the real-iPhone checklist
  (`.meridian/work/tether-mvp/g3-iphone-checklist.md`).
- W5 (native dock): the keyboard toggle does nothing in native (no `terminal` element is
  registered, so `FocusController.toggleKeyboard` has nothing to focus and the key row never
  shows), and native must report `Viewport.keyboardInset` (the keyboard frame's height).
- P3b: delete the `pointerdown` guard in `screens/terminal/terminals.ts` once the recognizer owns taps.
- P3b (iPad, touch mode, desktop layout): the top tools row (TabStrip pills, the "+" IconButton) uses
  ordinary buttons, so a tap blurs the owned input before `openDialog` runs, `held` is null and the
  keyboard does not return when the picker closes. Cancel `pointerdown` there when `directInput !== "xterm"`.
- P3b (nit): phone toasts rise by `--dock-height` on every phone screen; on Home and Files the bottom
  nav is `--toolbar-height`, so the toast-to-nav gap shrinks from about 16px to about 5px.
